WEBVTT

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.360
<i>Behold, the vast world in which we live!</i>

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:09.820
<i>It is rampant with monsters 
that threaten human life.</i>

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:16.320
<i>This threat is opposed by 
countless adventurers! Heroes!</i>

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.440
<i>Every day, they face these 
dangerous battles...</i>

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.580
<i>To protect the people! To protect the world!</i>

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.290
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.170
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.690
my journey continues!

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
My Healer!

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:15.150
<b>Despite the terrible time he's been having...</b>

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.810
There's something I've been wondering.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.640
What is it?

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.030
This is very out of the indigo.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.530
Are you really a healer?

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.700
I'm talking to <i>you</i>, Carla-san.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.410
Me? Of all people?

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.710
Who else could there be?

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.250
Where is this coming from?

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.630
Are you suggesting I'm not very healer-like?

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:40.870
What's not healery about me?

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.590
Everything?

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.500
But I'm so kind!

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.350
Objection.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.390
Overflowing with motherly instinct!

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:46.970
Objection.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.020
Who could ever doubt someone 
so soothing to the soul?!

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.470
Major bottleneck of objections here!

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.130
Then let me ask you a question, Alvin-san.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.360
What do you think a healer should be like?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.370
Let's see...

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.830
A healer should be kind and motherly...

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.620
Just being with them should 
be soothing to the soul!

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.560
Not even close, bud!

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.630
Why are you blushing?!

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.950
I've never even seen you 
use a single proper spell!

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.620
So if you saw me use one, 
you'd believe me then?

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.520
Would you mind if I broke 
a few of your ribs, then?

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.010
And there we are!

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.320
Behavior unbecoming of a healer!

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.500
But if you want me to use curative magic,

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.330
I need you to get hurt...

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.120
Then pick another—

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.890
Hey, look at that!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.900
Here I go! Off to slaughter humankind!

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.410
Young and old, men and women!

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.540
All shall fall to the bloodbath!

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.450
It's a monster.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:48.030
Bloodbath! Bloodbath!

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:46.880
And a fiendish one, at that.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.030
All right.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:50.380
I'll go fight him!

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.740
I see!

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:55.600
And then, after you die, I can resurrect you!

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.300
That's an interesting 
conclusion you jumped to.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:00.280
You think you can beat him, then?

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.810
Well... it might not be 
an easy victory, but...

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:07.290
In that case, cast an enhancement spell!

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.400
On the monster?! Are you a masochist?

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.420
On <i>me</i>!

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.430
But I'm not really sure that'll work...

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:16.530
What's this, now?

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.680
Are you saying you can't cast it?

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:23.220
I'm saying, anything times 
zero is still zero.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.450
What is that supposed to mean?!

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:28.910
But if that would prove to 
you that I'm a healer...

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.790
Wait, you <i>can</i> cast it?

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.220
Now, stand over there!

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:34.450
R-Right...

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:35.650
Go on, hop to it!

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.230
F-Fine...

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.130
Do I really need to be this far away?

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.010
I haven't done this in a while, 
so in case it goes wrong...

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:45.880
Hang on a minute!

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:46.980
What's going to go wrong?!

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:48.810
What are you expecting to go wrong?!

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:52.230
I think if I just pray... like this...

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.160
Hey, are you listening?!

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.470
I go like this, and...

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.240
I did it!

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.260
Hold it, hold it, hold it, hold it!

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.010
Now I throw it at you...

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.310
You throw it?!

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:07.250
That obvious manifestation of 
your black and twisted soul?!

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.740
Alvin-san!

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.130
There's no need to worry!

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:13.570
Are you sure?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.750
You'll be just fine!

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.620
I don't believe you!

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.790
Well? Are you convinced?

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:36.510
I'm convinced that you're unhinged!

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:47.310
Actually, there's something 
I've been wondering, too.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.830
It's a question that keeps me up at night.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.620
I guess you've got a lot more 
sleepless nights in store.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:59.080
Boy, I'm hungry.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.330
I guess it's just about lunchtime.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.330
<i>Stare...</i>

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:09.350
<i>Stare...</i>

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:15.350
<i>Stare...</i>

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.720
Fine, I'll ask!

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.350
Just stop staring like that!

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.670
So? What were you wondering about?

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.600
It's about you, Alvin-san!

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:28.620
Y-You mean... as a love interest?

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.730
I'm suing.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:31.230
Don't bring the law into this!

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.860
It was just a joke, anyway.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.220
What I'm wondering about is your strength.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.000
My strength?

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:41.460
You've claimed that your strength 
is on the level of a slug...

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.740
First I've heard of it.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.790
But the people who claim 
that they're the weakest

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:48.130
are often actually very strong!

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.110
Well, I'm genuinely not that strong...

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.270
Enough false modesty!

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:56.400
In order to properly gauge 
your slug-like strength,

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:58.770
I'd like you to fight this fellow here!

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:01.520
Yo!

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.070
Hey! You're the one from before!

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.020
You survived?

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:09.060
You can't die from an enhancement spell.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.280
Are you saying it was actually 
an enhancement spell?

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:15.050
Then why in the world did we 
hold that little funeral?

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.520
Surprised, are you?

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.780
Barely recognize me, do you?

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:21.610
Having endured that ominous 
enhancement spell,

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.040
and returned from the abyss of death,

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.700
I am truly unrecognizable!

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.560
So he <i>did</i> almost die!

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:31.320
The spell relies on the "what doesn't 
kill you makes you stronger" principle.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:32.390
Probably.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.560
Please don't cast spells 
based on speculation!

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:38.190
Well? Wanna fight?!

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.720
He seriously looks about the same as before.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:43.300
What exactly about him did you enhance?

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.340
His flavor.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.140
I might just stand a chance here.

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:54.160
H-Hang on a minute here!

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.700
Are you sure you didn't 
enhance anything else?

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.670
My toughness? My speed?!

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:02.560
Your mouthfeel, maybe?

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:03.830
You view me as an ingredient?

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.830
Were you just planning to 
eat me from the start?

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:07.910
Damn it!

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.430
That wasn't in my plan!

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:12.960
I won't be made your dinner's 
main dish that easily!

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.870
I'd love to boil you with rice!

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.590
What are you talking about?

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:18.500
Take this!

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:24.680
A smokescreen?!

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.100
No, this is...

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:27.970
Poison!

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.350
Alvin-san!

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.650
Fool! Stay back!

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:32.610
These are poisonous spores!

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.380
Did you say poison?

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.390
Indeed, it would be dangerous to approach...

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:41.750
Perhaps I'll just turn in for the day...

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.120
Come here, damn it!

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:47.590
One moment you're telling me 
to stay back, and the next...

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.260
What an unparalleled ego!

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.630
You've shown your true colors.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:53.620
Sad!

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:57.240
Look, I'm sorry about that.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:01.400
I didn't expect you to be so prepared 
that you even brought a gas mask!

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:06.780
Meanwhile, I'm shocked that you entered the 
forest without a single anti-poison measure.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:08.890
Are you an amateur?

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.340
I never expected you to 
best me in an argument.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:17.020
Damn. I must have breathed some in...

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.030
Are you all right?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.070
Do you have an antidote spell?

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:23.070
Yes, leave it to me.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.990
I'll put you out of your misery.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.380
That means <i>removing the poison</i>, right?

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.150
All jokes aside,

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:34.050
I <i>can</i> use an antidote spell,

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:38.310
but I'd prefer to preserve my magic power,

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.370
so I'll use an item instead.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.930
The antidote herbs we collected earlier?

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.630
Yes.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:48.830
Though I could also use some 
of those weeds over there.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.150
Why are you making this a choice?

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:54.720
I thought that adding choices 
might unlock a route split.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.030
A route split between dead or alive, maybe!

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:00.190
We don't need to go seeking out bad ends!

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:04.160
Hang on a minute. 
Why didn't that monster attack after—

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:08.040
<b>Poisooon</b>

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:08.040
Hey! What kind of monster 
succumbs to his own poison?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.490
And you didn't actually do anything!

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.730
It's a good thing he was 
such a stupid monster.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:20.070
Carla, cure my poison while he's down.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.170
Righty-o!

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:24.380
The pain...

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.560
Oh, the pain!

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.550
It hurts so much!

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:31.830
It just hurts so much!

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:33.300
It's talking.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:38.190
Monsters who live a long 
time acquire great wisdom,

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.530
and the ability to speak the human tongue!

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.080
We don't need that explanation again!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:44.660
Please... I don't wanna die yet...

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:45.780
Help me...

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.970
Help! I need somebody!

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.320
He does seem to want help, but...

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.340
If you could just give me the antidote—

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:55.580
Carla?

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:56.630
Hey!

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.850
W-Well...

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:01.900
Oh, that's right.

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:03.940
We were talking about attendants!

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:07.080
Very well. If that is your 
true heart's desire,

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:08.900
I will let you be my manservant!

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.100
<b>Manservant</b>

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.110
<i>Antidote</i>. An antidote for my poison!

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:16.510
You're thinking about 
helping him, aren't you?

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:17.490
Ack!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.320
<b>A
c
k</b>

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:20.000
O-Of course nack!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:19.700
<b>A
c
k</b>

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:24.310
H-He's a monster, and 
I'm not that foolack...

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:24.570
<b>A
c
k</b>

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:26.060
I've never been so annoyingly right.

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:28.770
For pity's sake.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:31.280
Is this more of your famed 
spirit of benevolence?

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:33.090
But have you considered the 
ramifications of your actions?

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:38.050
Even we save him, 
he might just attack us again!

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:43.060
And what's the guarantee that 
he won't attack someone else?

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:48.750
You heard him singing about 
slaughtering humans before!

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.730
The idea that you can achieve 
understanding with absolutely anybody

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.570
doesn't work in real life.

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:58.110
Is that... what you think?

00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:00.070
Well, it's what I keep saying...

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.760
Regardless, I'm still a holy woman...

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:08.700
I can't just sit back and watch 
while a life fades before my eyes.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.240
That thing's a monster.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:16.130
If you can't tell the difference...

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.620
Can't we just save him,

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:19.040
earn his gratitude,

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.740
and get him to give us 
lots of money and items?

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.390
That's just extortion!

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:26.770
Is that when you file a 
callus off your foot?

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:28.270
That's exfoliation.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:31.430
The thing you feel when you walk 
up three flights of stairs?

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:32.500
That's exertion.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.490
The process of a bird losing its feathers?

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:35.390
Exuviation!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:36.860
A die-off of species?

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:37.860
Extinction!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.160
And shut up!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:43.750
Hey...

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:44.900
What?

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:47.210
Doesn't it seem like you're over the poison?

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:49.250
Eh? Now that you mention it...

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:50.830
Tch. You caught on?

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:51.400
What?!

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:55.990
H-Hang on... I thought 
the poison took him out!

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:57.410
You fool!

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:01.070
That was all a performance 
to get your guard down!

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:04.390
A commonly-employed mushroom strategy,

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:06.740
to get you to approach so I 
could strike you unawares!

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.430
Then why didn't you stay down?

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.180
Tch.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.810
Thank goodness! 
You mean it was just a performance?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.520
I heard a tongue-click!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:18.140
I think you're just frustrated 
he stole your spotlight!

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:20.300
Is she really a holy woman?

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:22.460
That's what I'd like to know!

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:27.050
H-Hey, chill out, man...

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:29.370
I'll give you a great piece of info!

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:30.070
What is it?

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.850
That thing I did before 
was just a smokescreen.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:34.590
There was no poison in it.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.340
I mean, you sorta threw me for a loop there!

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:45.600
I send out one little smokescreen, 
and you start shouting "poisonous spores"!

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.120
I guess it had you under 
the weather for a bit,

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.590
but you seem to be feeling better now.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:51.800
Isn't that nice?

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:58.700
Are you saying you just 
assumed it was poison?

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.470
Goodness me... that can't be true, can it?

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:06.390
What's this? Why so quiet, eh?

00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:08.370
Go on, tell me! Don't be shy!

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:10.650
You're not some beginner.

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:14.110
You can't possibly have 
gotten that wrong, can you?

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:20.120
You little...

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:22.880
Hey! Cut it out!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.580
It's not nice to laugh 
at a person's mistakes!

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:32.920
<i>Hey... I don't think I've ever 
heard her laugh so hard before.</i>

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:35.270
<i>It's a damned trashy laugh, though...</i>

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:41.230
Good grief.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:44.740
<i>Maybe I'll just let it go this time.</i>

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.380
Okay, that's enough!

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:57.740
All that laughing got me hungry.

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:59.730
I'm pretty hungry too!

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:01.140
I've got an idea!

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:04.510
Let's all go off together to eat!

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:07.250
Anyone got any meal ideas?

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:08.500
Me!

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:10.730
I'd love some mushroom soup.

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:12.750
Or mushrooms boiled with rice.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:18.390
You really were planning to eat me, then?!

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:19.650
Damn it!

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:21.760
Wait, we're doing this again?!

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:25.420
I won't be made your dinner's 
main dish that easily!

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:28.100
After all that, we're back to square one?

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.110
I'd like you deep-fried, too.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.360
Since I did enhance your mouthfeel...

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.000
Don't play along!

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:41.280
Come, then! Try me!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.050
Fine, whatever...

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:45.000
All right.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:48.080
This was supposed to be a test 
of my strength from the start.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:54.210
Perhaps I'll give you a taste of my might!

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.230
Let's go!

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.270
Maybe I should have improved 
Alvin-san's mouthfeel instead.

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:36.090
Damn it...

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:41.100
I win!!

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:46.420
It's really coming down.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.980
I'm glad there was this cave nearby.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:52.760
Are you feeling any better, Alvin-san?

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.990
Alvin-san!

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.530
No!

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:00.010
The real me is right here!

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.430
Ow, ow...

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.770
You okay? I'm really sorry.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.750
I really lost my head back there.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:08.950
You've gotta take it easy, man. 
Chill out a minute.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.120
Being doted on by the person who beat me...

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:13.410
I'm so pathetic.

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:15.880
You are not!

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:20.590
At the very least, 
I think you're quite amazing!

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:22.580
I don't need your pity act.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:24.130
And don't throw my helmet!

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.760
It's not a pity act! 
I really think you're amazing!

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:30.220
To be as weak as you are and 
still become an adventurer...

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:31.800
That requires true mental fortitude!

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:32.990
Actually pity me!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:33.840
Now, now.

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:36.700
The whining will just make 
it worse! Calm down!

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.500
Stop making me sound like a sore loser!

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.910
I'll use a healing spell 
to make you better,

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.920
like I did with Mostly Bear-san.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:45.860
I can do that, because I'm a healer!

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:48.760
Are you still pretending you're a healer?

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:50.830
Of course I am!

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:53.630
And I'll shut that smart 
mouth of yours right now!

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.720
You really don't talk like someone 
about to make me better...

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:59.580
What got the worst of it?

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.580
The face, perhaps?

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.220
Probably your head!

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.920
That does look pretty bad.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:11.980
I did use a fa jin that would 
pierce through your armor...

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:13.090
Sorry, man.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:16.440
I didn't know you practiced martial arts!

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:18.830
Can you actually cure this?

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:20.290
What a worrywart.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:23.700
Have I ever betrayed your expectations?

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:25.890
Have you ever <i>met</i> them?

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:31.760
The preparations are complete!

00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:33.380
I wish you wouldn't dress like that!

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:42.640
Let my prayer be heard!

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.970
I really don't think that's 
going to cure anything...

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:47.520
Could you please stop?!

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:50.790
This is how I healed you when 
we stayed with Mostly Bear-san.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:52.540
I'm talking about appearances.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:55.730
Don't you have a less 
aggressive healing spell?

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.260
Well...

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.090
Is this better?

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:06.480
Can you really not do this 
without the cosplay?

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.940
Well, nothing seems broken.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.820
A simple spell would probably do the trick.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:15.730
Or maybe some medicinal herbs!

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:16.990
That's true.

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:20.090
Maybe medicinal herbs would be better 
than relying on some bizarre spell.

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:24.540
But if you use medicinal herbs, 
I can't prove my ability!

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:26.250
I'll try a chant!

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:30.260
I guess at some point we decided 
you'd be proving yourself, too.

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:32.490
Now, watch me.

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:37.320
With the miracles of God, 
it's easy to heal simple wounds like that!

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.820
Somehow, I'm not reassured.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.190
Now...

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:43.420
Great God above us,

00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:47.790
I beg of you, bring relief to the 
wounded body of the warrior, Alvin!

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:53.660
He may be pitiful, pathetic, hopeless, 
and utterly beyond saving...

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:53.660
Wait!

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:55.880
I beg of you, God!

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.800
I can no longer stand to see him like this!

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.680
Please, make him better!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:01.560
Enough!

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.990
Well? Are you better?

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:07.900
Of course not!

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:09.490
And don't click your tongue!

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:12.160
I-I wasn't clicking my tongue at you!

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:14.560
Who else would you be 
clicking your tongue at?!

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:18.440
At God, for not making you better...

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.810
That's blasphemous!

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:23.320
And at you, for not feeling better...

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.070
So it <i>was</i> at me!

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:27.190
And at the stupid slug.

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:29.460
That's also me—Hey, cut it out!

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:32.680
Hey, you guys!

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:35.850
I think the rain's let up.

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:41.700
It really has.

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:43.060
Ow...

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:45.090
And it was pouring just moments ago.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:50.360
Now that the weather's gotten better, 
we should probably head out.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:55.260
The weather... got better?

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:57.300
It got better?!

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:01.020
It definitely wasn't you!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.490
By the way...

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:13.420
why are you coming with us?

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:16.140
I'm so worried, I can't stay away.

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:17.760
I suppose you would be.

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:21.450
You'd be too worried to leave 
Alvin-san all on his own!

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:23.960
Don't pull yourself out of the firing range!

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:25.840
He's worried about you, too!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:29.900
And it'd be hard to get bored while 
I'm hanging out with you two.

00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:30.820
Mushroom-san.

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.930
Thank you for carrying my bag.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:34.270
Hey, no problem!

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:35.340
What's your name?

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:36.680
Altargaia!

00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:40.430
It's a pleasure to meet you, Altargaia-san.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:43.030
Isn't that a splendid name?

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:44.600
Much better than "Alvin."

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:47.560
You don't have to make it a competition!

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:27.300
Next episode's title is...

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:30.450
"The first dungeon Alvin tackles 
with Carla is designed for beginners

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:36.250
which is very nice and so even 
Alvin seems to be flying through it

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:38.500
but of course being the 
veteran rookie he is—"

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:40.050
<b>"The first dungeon Alvin tackles with Carla is designed for beginners
which is very nice and so even Alvin seems to be flying through it
but of course being the veteran rookie he is he isn't without his
struggles and he once again reveals his aptitude(?) for falling into holes
and even causes their mushroom monster companion to worry and
come to think of it the mushroom guy who showed up last episode
has a name (it's Altargaia) and there aren't many chances to call him
that but we would like you to remember it and by the way if you're
having trouble reading these titles to the end we just wanted to
remind you that you can pause the video or maybe check the show's
homepage and that's the deal with episode 4."</b>

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:40.000
Hey! I'm still talking—
